{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Ozen","id":"321508500138360843","is_bot":0,"username":"ozenannwn"},"author_id":"321508500138360843","channel_id":"746943529288466543","content":"It sounds like the setting is newly seeing a bit of an industrial revolution. How might the printing press effect things like spellbooks and perhaps wizard councils are very much against mass produced spellbooks making their craft too accessible? What are the effects of assembly line items perhaps squeezing other guilds out of their protected crafts?\n@BFDM is this another subplot you are interested in opening up within the setting as far as possible adventure hooks and the like?","created_at":"2020-08-25T00:13:25.066000Z","edited_at":"2020-08-25T00:19:04.055000Z","id":"747609543424344136","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"DM radar","id":"313689699627696139","is_bot":0,"username":"bfdm"},"author_id":"313689699627696139","channel_id":"746943529288466543","content":"I like the assembly line bit, but I'm not particularly interested in making a group that is against the printing press. Maybe its that I'm such a bibliophile. More books should be a good thing in my heart.","created_at":"2020-08-25T00:22:50.512000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"747611915076894781","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"DM radar","id":"313689699627696139","is_bot":0,"username":"bfdm"},"author_id":"313689699627696139","channel_id":"746943529288466543","content":"But the industrial revolution is what makes things like jenerous jack's vending machines possible","created_at":"2020-08-25T00:23:13.421000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"747612011164074116","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"DM radar","id":"313689699627696139","is_bot":0,"username":"bfdm"},"author_id":"313689699627696139","channel_id":"746943529288466543","content":"and is very much in line with the direction we are going.","created_at":"2020-08-25T00:23:24.108000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"747612055988600932","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"DM radar","id":"313689699627696139","is_bot":0,"username":"bfdm"},"author_id":"313689699627696139","channel_id":"746943529288466543","content":"The nearest historical analogue I can think of to the wizards not wanting magic books being published is the catholic church keeping bibles and masses in latin to prevent the people from gaining knowledge. This also is not something I want to recreate.","created_at":"2020-08-25T00:25:02.780000Z","edited_at":"2020-08-25T00:25:08.561000Z","id":"747612469849096224","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Ozen","id":"321508500138360843","is_bot":0,"username":"ozenannwn"},"author_id":"321508500138360843","channel_id":"746943529288466543","content":"I was thinking along the lines of there being fringe religious groups against the printing press mass producing the bible. Some priests were of the opinion that even if people could read the book they may not interpret it properly. \n\nI like the idea of portraying it in a good light while perhaps having a single antagonist or them and some minions arguing against it. In that way that there will always be people against a new thing. There are so many fun places to go with the idea that this one would be easy to leave alone.","created_at":"2020-08-25T01:29:44.179000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"747628749616316457","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"DM radar","id":"313689699627696139","is_bot":0,"username":"bfdm"},"author_id":"313689699627696139","channel_id":"746943529288466543","content":"There is probably some things we can do with magical printing. But maybe keep it in line with propaganda? Redcoats trying to stop the revolutionists from spreading the word.","created_at":"2020-08-25T01:34:35.434000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"747629971228327956","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
